export anchor CycleComputerStyle:
    number: 389
    screen: FitnessTracker
    name: Cycle computer
    idea: The day shown on two pages of a handlebar computer, a moulded housing with hardware buttons around a dark LCD split by hard lines into data fields, each with a tiny caps label, a huge digit and a unit.
    base: dark
    palette:
        page: #0c0d0e, the page behind the devices and the style sheet
        housing: #1c1e21, the moulded device body, nav pills and sheet labels
        housingHigh: #2a2d31, the lit top of the housing and the secondary button
        bezel: #060707, the black frame around the screen
        lcd: #0f1612, the screen and every data field
        cellLine: #2c3d33, the 2px lines that split the fields
        ink: #e3f3d2, digits, bars and lit segments
        muted: #9fb79a, field labels, units and rest days
        dim: #3d5446, unlit segments
        amber: #ffb648, the saved alert, the top zone, today, the current page and the primary button
        onAmber: #231503, text on amber
    type:
        Digits and labels use DIN Alternate, Bahnschrift, Roboto Mono, ui-
        monospace, Menlo, Consolas, bold with tabular numbers. The distance
        field is 88px, standard fields 54px, small fields 40px, units 15px
        muted, field labels 11px caps tracked 0.12em. Page text uses Segoe
        UI, Roboto, system-ui at 14px.
    layout:
        A plain header with Brightwork Move, Today and the date, and Today,
        Week and Plan as round pills with Today in amber. Below, two device
        housings side by side, each a 36px rounded moulded body with side
        hardware buttons, a page label and page dots at the top and three
        key labels at the bottom. Page 1 is the Evening run. Its screen has
        a status strip with Run saved, the date and signal bars, an amber
        alert bar with a flag reading Run done 8.2 km saved, then a field
        grid on six columns split by 2px lines. A full width Distance field
        shows 8.2 km at 88px. Then Time, Avg pace, Avg HR and Avg speed in
        half width fields, the speed of 11.6 km per h derived from distance
        and time. Then a full width Time in zone field with five bars,
        minutes on top, zone 3 in amber and Z labels below. Page 2 is Day
        and week. Move, Exercise and Stand each take a third with percent,
        value over goal, a segment gauge and the amount to go. A full width
        Distance this week field draws seven bars with figures, rest days as
        a dashed floor with a dash, two letter day names and a triangle on
        Saturday. Then Sleep 7 h 12 min with deep 1 h 34 min, the Half
        marathon at week 6 of 12 with a twelve segment gauge, and a full
        width Next session field reading 14 km long run tomorrow. Below
        1060px the devices stack. At 375px values shrink to 34px and half
        width fields stay in pairs.
    spacing: An 8px unit. Fields packed with 2px divider lines and 8 to 12px padding, 28px between devices.
    density: High. Every figure gets its own field, the run on page 1 and the day on page 2.
    corners: 36px on the housing, 12px on the screen, square fields, round page dots and pills.
    borders: 2px lines between fields and a 6px black bezel around the screen.
    shadows: A deep drop shadow under the housing, a highlight on its top edge and inset shade on the screen and hardware keys.
    icons:
        A flag in the saved alert, signal bars in the status strip, page
        dots and segment gauges for rings and plan. Rest days are a dashed
        floor with a dash and today carries a triangle.
    focus: A 3px amber outline offset 2px.
    tone: Device labels such as Avg pace, Time in zone, Run done and Next session.
